voxelslam.cpp -- the Voxel-SLAM node implementation.

One patch per upstream file, so this patch carries every bridge change to
voxelslam.cpp. Every hunk explains its rationale in the staged source with a
`voxelslam_bridge:` tag; this numbered header is the concern-level index.

1. Capture upstream odometry, deskewed scans, loop decisions, GBA metrics, and
   the finalized optimized path for the offline result API.
2. Make gravity alignment, covariance rotation, and convergence calculations
   well-defined for aligned vectors and zero/short residual inputs.
3. Make cross-thread loop/reset flags atomic and expose stable worker/ticket
   lifecycle state, including initialization, degradation, and reset outcomes.
4. Suppress ROS subscriptions in the Python module and gate both map-output
   directory creation sites on the existing `is_save_map` option.
5. Remove stale slide-map pointers when their owning octrees are released.
6. Preserve loop-closure acceptance behavior while recording each gate and
   ensure the loop busy flag clears on every iteration exit.
7. Refuse undersized GBA windows before code that assumes two states.
8. Order the global-bundle-adjustment thread against the offline host: publish a
   drained-idle flag the host can wait on, and admit a bottom-up pass only
   between loop-closure iterations, so how many passes land before a given sweep
   -- and therefore gba_edges1 and the finalized path -- stops depending on host
   scheduling. A session reset publishes its completion the same way: the reset
   flag the host also tests clears only after the new session and that drained
   flag are installed, so no all-idle state is observable mid-reset.
9. Close the keyframe races the single mutex left open: make history_kfsize
   atomic, install a pose-graph result as one critical section, and take the
   keyframe mutex in keyframe_loading and around every session swap -- covering
   both per-session vectors, keyframes and scan poses, because the global-BA
   thread indexes each of them under that mutex.
10. Move the travelled-distance map prune out of the odometry thread's idle
   branch, where wall-clock pacing chose the sweep it ran on, into the per-sweep
   path.
11. Let an externally supplied odometry prior predict each sweep in place of IMU
   dead reckoning -- during initialization as well as steady state -- and stand
   in for the whole state when the IEKF reports a degenerate update, so
   degenerate geometry does not accumulate toward a reset and no part of the
   rejected solve survives it. Report how often it did both. The same prior
   lifts motion_init's degeneracy veto, but only while its local-BA factor is
   installed: seeding a solve does not change the rank of its normal equations,
   so covering the window in time is not the same as constraining it.
12. Replace fractional POSIX sleep calls, which truncate to zero and busy-spin,
   with explicit chrono durations, and take them only on iterations that found
   no work, so consuming a keyframe no longer costs a poll interval. These waits
   throttle only genuinely idle online workers; offline synchronization still
   depends solely on published queue/processing/drained state.

13. Give the keyframe gate a dwell-time release, so a platform that stands still
   long enough is still described. Upstream releases a keyframe only on
   displacement, which leaves a long stationary start with no descriptor at all
   and makes the start-to-end closure -- the only one that observes the whole
   accumulated drift -- undetectable. Off by default.

14. Report out of the odometry IEKF the two things it already computes and
   discards -- the full `nnt` eigenvalue triple and the match count -- and take
   the per-sweep disagreement between the odometry prior's prediction and what
   registration made of it. Purely diagnostic: the triple is the only window
   into why upstream's `eigenvalues[0] < 14` verdict fired, which is what drives
   the degenerate fallback and the resets, and the disagreement is the only
   measure of what registration adds over the prior that survives that fallback.
   Nothing in the estimator reads either back.

15. Summarize the IMU-propagated prediction covariance per sweep before the
   prior's pose block replaces it and its cross terms are cleared, since neither
   is recoverable afterwards. Also diagnostic, and also read by nothing: it says
   whether the constant the prior's sigma is tuned to stands in for something
   that actually moves, and how much information the substitution discards.

Hunks are generated with `diff -U3` and applied with `patch -F0 -p0`; missing
context is therefore rejected as upstream drift rather than accepted with fuzz.

